DEVELOPMENT PLANS

Tamlinux is an independent Linux workstation environment. The package remains
tamlinux; its terminal command is tam. A plan describes work and acceptance,
not an installed component.

Status (2026-11-02): Product develop is KBN WB 0.6.1 (VERSION <../../VERSION>,
CULTIVAR <../../CULTIVAR>). Gate A closed with released 0.4.8 (2026-10-22) and
Blue Sparkler 0.5.12 released on 2026-11-01; Arch/Hyprland remains the current
host. Candidate assemblies and deployment live in tamlinux-packages
<https://github.com/greenermoose/tamlinux-packages>.

This index lists open product plans only. Finished Gate A / 0.4.3–0.4.4 plans
and dated evidence are in Git; see <FILING-CARD.md>. Do not treat filing-card
entries as current guidance.

Stage and branch rules for public repos are in VERSIONING.md
<../../VERSIONING.md>. Full stage policy (who may move Test, Run, and Release)
is private operating procedure, not duplicated here.

  Plan: Steady active monitor <steady-active-monitor.md>
  Current scope: Approved 2026-11-10: timestamped output diagnostics,
  active-display continuity during side-monitor wake, and selective old-log
  cleanup. Develop pending.

  Plan: Easy workstation upgrades <workstation-upgrade.md>
  Current scope: Approved 2026-10-30: released-assembly upgrades and recovery.

  Plan: Input usability <input-usability.md>
  Current scope: Approved for 0.5 (K22–K25): modifier model, clipboard,
  titlebar close.

  Plan: Keybinding usability <keybinding-usability.md>
  Current scope: Open 0.5 binding and explorer work.

  Plan: Text macros and Meta naming <text-macros-and-meta.md>
  Current scope: Complete desktop-wide macro delivery, reserve Meta+Alt, unify
  naming and package the trial.

  Plan: Start menu <start-menu.md>
  Current scope: Combined Quick Launch + Settings; packaged acceptance
  pending.

  Plan: Console-first startup <console-first-startup.md>
  Current scope: Text login; optional desktop via tam-desktop.

  Plan: Console welcome <console-welcome.md>
  Current scope: Console greeting and first-run messaging.

  Plan: First login activities <first-login-activities.md>
  Current scope: First text-login orientation (hi) and activities (start)
  (D214, D215).

  Plan: Targeted text-console monitors <console-monitor-control.md>
  Current scope: Console fb mapping and native monitor CLI/TUI.

  Plan: Native input startup <native-input-startup.md>
  Current scope: Input stack at session start.

  Plan: Remove screensaver <remove-screensaver.md>
  Current scope: Retire screensaver paths.

  Plan: Theme system <theme-system.md>
  Current scope: Retained theme ownership; Tamarack redesign in 0.5.

  Plan: Fleet <fleet.md>
  Current scope: Registered-host deploy and fleet tools.

  Plan: nftables host firewall <nftables-host-firewall.md>
  Current scope: 0.6 D204: owned nftables, SSH helpers, ufw removal after
  cutover.

  Plan: tam-hardware <tam-hardware.md>
  Current scope: Host CPU/ISA/DMI probe for agents (D209).

  Plan: tam-meter <tam-meter.md>
  Current scope: Unprivileged C energy meter and live view (D191).

  Plan: tam-boot <tam-boot.md>
  Current scope: Startup explainer and diagnostics tool (K40, K60).

  Plan: tam command <tamlinux-command.md>
  Current scope: Workstation plan for the separate tam component.

  Plan: Compositor protocol layer <compositor-protocol-layer.md>
  Current scope: Protocol facade; Sway adapter later.

  Plan: Sway integration <sway-integration.md>
  Current scope: After dependable Hyprland baseline (0.7+).

  Plan: Base operating system <base-operating-system.md>
  Current scope: Second distro, then Void pilot.

  Plan: Operating-system horizons <operating-system-horizons.md>
  Current scope: Research only; chooses no base.

  Plan: Retire hey <retire-hey.md>
  Current scope: Remove remaining hey identifiers.

Product behavior and generic defaults belong here. Exact assemblies belong in
tamlinux-packages; personal selections belong in consumer config. New Develop
source needs its own exact delivery selection; moving source does not
establish runtime parity.
